# Keep the agent's runtime records byte-stable across machines.
#
# The scan log is appended to by whichever machine is running the scan: a
# Windows laptop writes CRLF line endings, a Linux GitHub Actions runner writes
# LF. Without this, every scheduled run would look like it had rewritten the
# whole file, producing enormous meaningless diffs and pointless push conflicts.
# Forcing LF means a diff shows only the lines actually added.
scan_log.jsonl text eol=lf
processed_files.json text eol=lf

# Sample contracts and policies are plain text the agent reads; normalise them
# too so a document's fingerprint does not change just because it was checked
# out on a different operating system.
*.txt text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Test fixtures are binary — never touch their bytes.
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
